69
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:41.000
the Marines had a strict protocol they followed. When the military police spoke with Raheel, he elaborated on what had upset him. He couldn't handle drill instructors yelling at him and hitting him. The instructors dismissed Raheel's claims. They hadn't hit him, they had only touched him when they had to provide corrections, such as fixing his uniform or position. Drill instructors were barred from touching recruits in all situations, except to drill corrections. It was determined that Raheel should remain on the base under Suicide Watch.
海军陆战队有一套严格的协议。当宪兵与拉希尔交谈时，他详细说明了让他心烦意乱的原因。他无法忍受教官对他大喊大叫并打他。教官们驳回了拉希尔的说法。他们没有打他，只有在必须提供纠正时才触碰他，例如整理他的制服或姿势。教官在所有情况下都被禁止触碰新兵，除非是进行纠正训练。最终决定拉希尔应留在基地接受自杀监视。

70
00:31:41.000 --> 00:32:37.000
Recruits were only transported off base for treatment if they had actually self-harmed or attempted suicide. Raheel was moved to another platoon's squad bay and was told to sit on a mattress in the middle of the room. He sat there for 24 hours while other recruits took it in turns to watch over him. When night fell, they shone a torch into his face in order to keep an eye on him. Eventually, Raheel spoke up and said he'd changed his mind. He didn't want to die at all. He wanted to continue training and become a Marine. The next morning, Raheel's senior drill instructor, Gunnery Sergeant Joseph Felix, took Raheel to recruit liaison services to discuss the previous day's events with a higher up.
只有在实际自残或企图自杀的情况下，新兵才会被送出基地接受治疗。拉希尔被转移到另一个排的宿舍，并被告知坐在房间中间的床垫上。他在那里坐了 24 小时，其他新兵轮流看守他。夜幕降临时，他们用手电筒照向他的脸，以便监视他。最终，拉希尔开口说他改变了主意。他根本不想死。他想继续训练并成为一名海军陆战队员。第二天早上，拉希尔的高级教官，炮兵军士约瑟夫·费利克斯，带拉希尔去新兵联络处与上级讨论前一天发生的事情。

71
00:32:37.000 --> 00:33:23.000
Usually drill instructors waited outside for recruits for meetings like this, but Felix stayed in the office throughout about 10 feet away from Raheel. Raheel explained that he had no intention of killing himself and had no history of mental health problems. He had only said that because he wanted the training to stop. This recruit thought it was the only way to quit. The recruit never meant that and regrets it. Raheel was dismissed as a low risk for self-harm and returned to his platoon. Over the next few days, the recruits continued training. They had to perform sprints and cross-country runs.
通常教官会在外面等新兵参加这样的会议，但费利克斯一直待在办公室里，距离拉希尔大约 10 英尺。拉希尔解释说他没有自杀的意图，也没有心理健康问题的病史。他之所以那样说，只是因为他想停止训练。这个新兵认为这是退出的唯一途径。该新兵从未那样想过，并对此感到后悔。拉希尔被认为自残风险较低，并回到了他的排。在接下来的几天里，新兵们继续训练。他们必须进行短跑和越野跑。

72
00:33:23.000 --> 00:34:05.000
They were taught mixed martial arts, bayonet techniques and close-order drills. During one routine focused on punching, recruits were split into pairs and instructed to punch one another repeatedly. Many of the larger, stronger recruits were teamed up with smaller individuals. They were told not to listen to their DI's instructions just to keep punching. Many recruits were hidden their jaws. One suffered broken ribs, another broke down in tears. Drill instructors would refer to their recruits as maggots, pussies and a variety of sexist and homophobic slurs.
他们学习了综合格斗、刺刀技术和队列训练。在一次专注于出拳的例行训练中，新兵们被分成两人一组，并被指示反复击打对方。许多体型较大、较强壮的新兵与体型较小的人配对。他们被告知不要听教官的指示，只需继续出拳。许多新兵被打得下巴受伤。一人肋骨骨折，另一人泪流满面。教官们会称呼他们的新兵为“蛆虫”、“懦夫”，以及各种性别歧视和恐同的侮辱性词汇。

73
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:53.000
Some were targeted for their personal attributes such as their ethnicity. Drill instructors themselves weren't immune from abuse either. Senior DI's would often yell at their subordinates who in turn took out their anger on recruits. After Gunnery Sergeant Joseph Felix shouted at one DI, he began screaming at his recruits to the extent that he became sick and vomited across the floor. One of Raheel Siddiqui's platoon mates noticed that Raheel seemed baffled by being asked to follow orders. Following orders was crucial to being in the Marines, but Raheel seemed to query why he was being told to do certain things.
有些人因个人属性（如种族）而成为目标。教官们自己也无法免受虐待。高级教官经常对下属大喊大叫，下属反过来又把愤怒发泄在新兵身上。在炮兵军士约瑟夫·费利克斯对一名教官大喊大叫后，他开始对他的新兵尖叫，以至于他生病并呕吐在地板上。拉希尔·西迪基的一名排友注意到，拉希尔似乎对被要求服从命令感到困惑。服从命令对于成为海军陆战队员至关重要，但拉希尔似乎质疑为什么他被告知要做某些事情。

74
00:34:53.000 --> 00:35:44.000
His platoon mate wondered why he had enlisted and later told the New York Times that Raheel always looked like a scared animal. At about 2am on Friday March 18, the recruit who shared Raheel's bunk was woken by Raheel. He wanted to talk to him, explaining that he was in pain. Where all in pain, his bunk mate replied before turning over to go back to sleep. Two hours later it was time for the recruits to get up. By 4.15 they were lined up to go to breakfast. A drill instructor told them to sound off before they left, a term used for the call Marines are required to give in response to an order.
他的排友想知道他为什么要入伍，后来告诉《纽约时报》，拉希尔看起来总是像一只受惊的动物。3 月 18 日星期五凌晨 2 点左右，与拉希尔共用一张床铺的新兵被拉希尔叫醒。他想和他谈谈，解释说他很痛苦。“我们都很痛苦，”他的床友回答，然后翻身继续睡觉。两个小时后，新兵们该起床了。到 4 点 15 分，他们排队去吃早餐。一名教官告诉他们在离开前“报数”（sound off），这是海军陆战队员在响应命令时被要求发出的呼喊。

75
00:35:44.000 --> 00:36:22.000
All except Raheel obeyed. Two DI's noticed and began to yell at him for disobeying orders. When one approached Raheel and demanded he sound off, Raheel pointed at his throat and silently passed him a note. It read, This recruit has to go to medical. This recruits throat has been swollen for three days and is getting worse. This recruit also coughed blood a few times last night, and this recruit completely lost his voice and can barely whisper.
除了拉希尔，所有人都服从了。两名教官注意到了，并开始对他不服从命令大喊大叫。当其中一人接近拉希尔并要求他报数时，拉希尔指着自己的喉咙，默默地递给他一张纸条。上面写着：“这个新兵必须去医疗单位。这个新兵的喉咙已经肿了三天，而且越来越严重。这个新兵昨晚还咳了几次血，而且这个新兵完全失去了声音，几乎只能耳语。”

76
00:36:22.000 --> 00:37:07.000
This recruits whole neck is in a lot of pain. The drill instructor told Raheel they'd sought him out after breakfast. In the meantime Raheel would have to go to the mess hall with the rest of his platoon. At breakfast a drill instructor asked for Raheel's help passing out cups. Raheel ignored him. He sat quietly as the rest of the platoon ate, staring into space. By 5.30 am the platoon was back at their barracks doing some cleaning. Raheel was ordered to the front of the squad bay so he could fill out a form to go to the medical unit.
“这个新兵的整个脖子都很痛。”教官告诉拉希尔，他们早餐后会找他。在此期间，拉希尔必须和排里的其他人一起去食堂。早餐时，一名教官要求拉希尔帮忙分发杯子。拉希尔无视了他。他静静地坐着，看着排里的其他人吃饭，盯着虚空。到早上 5 点 30 分，排里回到了营房进行清理。拉希尔被命令到宿舍前面，以便他可以填写表格去医疗单位。

77
00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:57.000
When Raheel approached senior drill instructor Joseph Felix, Raheel didn't address him as was required, presumably due to his sore throat. Instead he stood there silently. Felix became angry and demanded Raheel run get-backs across the squad bay. This involved sprinting back and forth across the length of the room until told to stop. Exercise such as this was known as incentive training. Raheel did as he was told while holding his throat as Felix continued to shout, Siddiqui run get-back run I don't care what's wrong with you you're going to say something back to me.
当拉希尔接近高级教官约瑟夫·费利克斯时，拉希尔没有按照要求称呼他，大概是因为他喉咙痛。相反，他默默地站在那里。费利克斯变得愤怒，并要求拉希尔在宿舍里跑“折返跑”（get-backs）。这包括在房间长度上来回冲刺，直到被告知停止。这种运动被称为“激励训练”。拉希尔照做了，同时捂着喉咙，而费利克斯继续大喊：“西迪基，跑折返跑，跑！我不在乎你怎么了，你得回我话。”

78
00:37:57.000 --> 00:38:36.000
The other recruits kept cleaning quietly as Raheel ran back and forth across the squad bay. Then suddenly Raheel clutched his throat and fell to the floor crying. He lay there motionless his hands still wrapped around his neck. Get up Siddiqui I know you're faking yelled Felix get up. Get up. He walked over to Raheel and slapped him across the face. Raheel's head turned to one side but otherwise he didn't move. Felix slapped him again.
其他新兵安静地继续清理，而拉希尔在宿舍里来回奔跑。然后突然，拉希尔捂住喉咙，哭着倒在地板上。他躺在那里一动不动，双手仍然紧紧抓着脖子。“起来，西迪基，我知道你在装模作样，”费利克斯大喊，“起来。起来。”他走到拉希尔身边，扇了他一巴掌。拉希尔的头转向一边，但除此之外他没有动。费利克斯又扇了他一巴掌。

79
00:38:36.000 --> 00:39:33.000
He did it so forcefully that the sound echoed across the enormous squad bay. Raheel stood up holding his face and began running again. One of his platoon mates thought it was the fastest he'd ever seen anyone run before. It looked as though Raheel was completing the get-backs he'd been ordered to do. But then he kept running to the back of the room where a set of double doors led to an external staircase. Raheel pushed the doors open and hoisted himself up on the railing of the stairway. Then his feet caught on the metal rail and he tumbled over the side. At 5.35am a marine who happened to be outside passing by saw Raheel's body fall from the third floor and hit the concrete below.
他用力之大，声音在巨大的宿舍区回荡。拉希尔捂着脸站起来，又开始奔跑。他的一名排友认为这是他见过跑得最快的一次。看起来拉希尔是在完成被命令做的折返跑。但随后他继续跑到房间后面，那里有一组双开门通向外部楼梯。拉希尔推开门，把自己拉到楼梯的栏杆上。接着他的脚被金属栏杆绊住，翻过了侧面。凌晨5点35分，一名恰好路过的海军陆战队员看到拉希尔的身体从三楼坠落，撞击在下方的混凝土上。

80
00:39:33.000 --> 00:40:20.000
The marine called 911 and reported, I got a recruit that fell from the third deck. Meanwhile up in the squad bay Raheel's shocked platoon mates were ordered to file into the bathroom and face the wall. While Raheel was being given first aid they were taken to complete their usual training schedule. Drill instructors warned them not to talk about what they'd seen. Raheel had suffered severe blunt force trauma but was still alive. An air ambulance was requested to take him to a hospital 40 miles away. Due to heavy fog an airlift wasn't possible so the Marines drove Raheel to Beaufort Memorial Hospital.
这名海军陆战队员拨打了911并报告说，我有一名新兵从三楼掉下来了。与此同时，在宿舍区，拉希尔震惊的排友们被命令排队进入浴室并面对墙壁。在拉希尔接受急救时，他们被带去完成日常训练计划。教官警告他们不要谈论所见之事。拉希尔遭受了严重的钝器伤，但仍有生命体征。一架空中救护车被要求将他送往40英里外的医院。由于大雾，空运无法实现，海军陆战队便开车将拉希尔送往博福特纪念医院。

81
00:40:20.000 --> 00:41:13.000
For an hour emergency room doctors worked on Raheel. They realized that he needed a more specialized form of care so he was transferred to another hospital in Charleston. Gazala Siddiqui hadn't stopped worrying about her son since he left home for boot camp. She'd only had one bizarre phone call from him and hadn't been able to talk to him at all. At 7pm on Friday March 18, a week and a half after that call, there was a knock on the front door of the Siddiqui residence. Gazala answered the door to see two Marines standing outside. Gazala assumed they must be there to share some good news about her son's achievements at training. The thought was a relief.
急诊室医生为拉希尔抢救了一个小时。他们意识到他需要更专业的护理，于是将他转院到查尔斯顿的另一家医院。加扎拉·西迪基自从儿子离家去新兵训练营后就一直担心不已。她只接到过他一个奇怪的电话，之后就再也没能和他通话。3月18日星期五晚上7点，也就是那通电话后的一个半星期，西迪基家的前门被敲响了。加扎拉开门看到两名海军陆战队员站在外面。加扎拉以为他们一定是来分享关于她儿子在训练中取得成就的好消息的。这个想法让她感到宽慰。

82
00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:56.000
She had been worried about Raheel since he'd gone away to the extent that she'd struggled to sleep at night. Gazala invited the Marines inside. The two officers stepped inside and asked if everyone was at home. Gazala said that she and her daughter Sidra were there but her husband Masoud was at work. One of the officers stepped back outside and made a brief phone call. As he was talking, Sidra overheard him say, The dad's not home now, should I still say it? Sidra was confused and couldn't understand what was happening.
自从拉希尔离开后，她一直很担心，以至于晚上难以入睡。加扎拉邀请海军陆战队员进屋。两名军官走进屋内，询问是否所有家人都在家。加扎拉说她和女儿西德拉在家，但丈夫马苏德在上班。其中一名军官退到外面，打了一个简短的电话。在他通话时，西德拉无意中听到他说，父亲现在不在家，我还要说吗？西德拉感到困惑，无法理解发生了什么。

83
00:41:56.000 --> 00:42:43.000
The officer returned and said to Gazala, Ma'am, I have bad news. Your son passed away. In total disbelief, Gazala replied, No, no, no. You're wrong. You're wrong. Something is wrong. Then she cried out for Sidra to call her father before fainting. When Gazala woke, she was in the hospital being treated for shock. Despite the best efforts of doctors in South Carolina, Raheel had been pronounced dead at 10.06am, four and a half hours after his fall. His death was ruled a suicide.
那名军官回来后对加扎拉说，女士，我有坏消息。你的儿子去世了。加扎拉完全不相信，回答说，不，不，不。你错了。你错了。一定是哪里搞错了。然后她哭喊着让西德拉叫她父亲，随后昏倒了。当加扎拉醒来时，她正在医院接受休克治疗。尽管南卡罗来纳州的医生尽了最大努力，拉希尔还是在上午10点06分被宣布死亡，距离他坠楼过去了四个半小时。他的死被裁定为自杀。

84
00:42:43.000 --> 00:43:47.000
Almost a week later on Thursday, March 24, Raheel's body was flown home to Michigan in a coffin draped with an American flag. When the Siddiqi family viewed his body at the funeral home, they were horrified by what they saw. There were ligature marks around his neck, and most of his body had a purpleish hue. When the family read Raheel's autopsy report, they noticed that in addition to the blunt force trauma, the forensic pathologist found evidence of particular hemorrhaging. This could be caused by heavy coughing or vomiting, or even strangulation. Despite the coroner's ruling of suicide, the Siddiqi's couldn't believe Raheel had taken his own life. They felt his devotion to his parents would make it impossible for him to do so, as well as his Islamic faith, which considered suicide a sin.
近一周后的3月24日星期四，拉希尔的遗体被运回密歇根州，棺材上覆盖着美国国旗。当西迪基一家在殡仪馆瞻仰他的遗体时，他们被所见景象惊呆了。他的脖子上有勒痕，大部分身体呈紫红色。当家人阅读拉希尔的尸检报告时，他们注意到除了钝器伤外，法医病理学家还发现了点状出血的证据。这可能是由剧烈咳嗽、呕吐甚至勒颈引起的。尽管验尸官裁定为自杀，但西迪基一家无法相信拉希尔会自杀。他们认为他对父母的孝顺使他不可能这样做，而且他的伊斯兰信仰也将自杀视为罪孽。

85
00:43:47.000 --> 00:44:53.000
Certain there was more to the situation than met the eye, they retained a lawyer to advocate on their behalf. When officials interviewed the Siddiqi's, they confirmed that Raheel had no history of mental illness. He had always been well-behaved with a mischievous sense of humour, and their memory of him was as a son who smiled all the time. Upon hearing the story of how Raheel had died, the Siddiqi's and their lawyer were unsettled. They couldn't understand how so many witnesses in the squad bay had seen Raheel collapse and be slapped by Felix, yet only one individual had detailed how he had fallen. An investigation into Raheel's death began. It was coordinated by the Paris Island Office of the Naval Criminal Investigative Service, also known as NCIS. While they were adamant that there were no indications of foul play, they still wanted to gain a full understanding of the events that led up to Raheel's death.
他们确信情况远非表面看起来那么简单，于是聘请了一名律师代表他们。当官员采访西迪基一家时，他们证实拉希尔没有精神疾病史。他一直表现良好，有着调皮的幽默感，在他们的记忆中，他是一个总是面带微笑的儿子。在听到拉希尔死亡的经过后，西迪基一家和他们的律师感到不安。他们无法理解为什么宿舍区有那么多目击者看到拉希尔倒下并被菲利克斯扇耳光，却只有一个人详细描述了他坠楼的过程。针对拉希尔死亡的调查开始了。调查由海军刑事调查局（NCIS）的帕里斯岛办公室协调。虽然他们坚称没有迹象表明存在谋杀，但他们仍希望全面了解导致拉希尔死亡的事件。

86
00:44:53.000 --> 00:46:03.000
Although the investigation would look at Paris Island as a whole, it was primarily focused on the third recruit training battalion. Much of the investigation's focus was on gunnery Sergeant Joseph Felix, who had been Raheel's senior drill instructor. Aged in his 30s, Felix had enlisted in the Marines in 2002. During his 14 years of service, he had worked as an air traffic controller and was deployed to the Iraq and Afghanistan wars. His time there left a lasting impact on him. Felix would rant to other Marines about how he hated Muslims, blaming them for killing friends who'd served alongside him. While it is unclear whether Joseph Felix suffered PTSD following his service in war zones, one officer told the New York Times he had a reputation for being, quote, pretty freaking psycho. One of the more aggressive drill instructors in his company, he even scared recruits who weren't in his platoon.
虽然调查将审视整个帕里斯岛，但重点主要集中在第三新兵训练营。调查的大部分焦点集中在炮兵中士约瑟夫·菲利克斯身上，他是拉希尔的高级教官。菲利克斯30多岁，于2002年加入海军陆战队。在他14年的服役期间，他曾担任空中交通管制员，并被派往伊拉克和阿富汗战争。在那里的经历对他产生了持久的影响。菲利克斯会向其他海军陆战队员抱怨他有多讨厌穆斯林，指责他们杀害了与他并肩作战的朋友。虽然不清楚约瑟夫·菲利克斯在战区服役后是否患有创伤后应激障碍（PTSD），但一名军官告诉《纽约时报》，他以“相当疯狂”而闻名。作为连队里最激进的教官之一，他甚至吓坏了不在他排里的新兵。

87
00:46:03.000 --> 00:47:01.000
One recruit who'd been training in Raheel Siddiqui's cohort saw Felix push another recruit into a footlocker. Others were choked or thrown against walls. On one occasion, Felix forced a recruit to only eat jelly and mashed potatoes for several days. And it appeared that Felix had a history of singling out Muslim recruits in particular. In 2015, the year before Raheel Siddiqui began training, Felix had repeatedly tormented a young Muslim from Brooklyn named Amir Bormash. As well as accusing him of being a terrorist spy, Felix forced Amir into an industrial dryer, then turned it on. And Amir wasn't the only victim. That same year, Felix honed in on a 19-year-old named Rakan Harvez.
一名在拉希尔·西迪基同批次训练的新兵看到菲利克斯把另一名新兵推入储物柜。其他人则被掐住脖子或被扔向墙壁。有一次，菲利克斯强迫一名新兵连续几天只吃果冻和土豆泥。而且菲利克斯似乎有专门针对穆斯林新兵的历史。2015年，也就是拉希尔·西迪基开始训练的前一年，菲利克斯曾多次折磨一名来自布鲁克林的年轻穆斯林阿米尔·博马什。除了指责他是恐怖分子间谍外，菲利克斯还强迫阿米尔进入工业烘干机，然后将其打开。阿米尔并不是唯一的受害者。同年，菲利克斯盯上了一名19岁的年轻人拉坎·哈维兹。

88
00:47:01.000 --> 00:48:06.000
Rakan had immigrated to the United States from Kurdistan with his family as a baby. Felix nicknamed Rakan terrorist, ISIS, and Kurdish. Like Amir, Rakan was forced into a dryer by Felix, although he didn't switch it on. Despite the ethos of what happens in 3rd Battalion stays in 3rd Battalion, these incidents hadn't gone unreported. When recruit Jake Weaver was told in 2015 that he would be receiving an other-than-honorable discharge from the Marines, his father decided to step in. Troy Weaver had been told by his son about the abuses that had gone on at Parris Island. It seemed incredibly unfair that Jake would be receiving a bad discharge after what he'd seen and experienced. Troy Weaver contacted Jake's commanding officer and shared what he knew.
拉坎婴儿时期随家人从库尔德斯坦移民到美国。菲利克斯给拉坎起了“恐怖分子”、“ISIS”和“库尔德人”等绰号。像阿米尔一样，拉坎也被菲利克斯强迫进入烘干机，尽管他没有打开开关。尽管有“第三营发生的事就留在第三营”的潜规则，但这些事件并非没有被举报。当新兵杰克·韦弗在2015年被告知他将因非荣誉退伍而离开海军陆战队时，他的父亲决定介入。特洛伊·韦弗从儿子那里得知了帕里斯岛发生的虐待事件。在经历了所见所闻后，杰克被非荣誉退伍显得极其不公平。特洛伊·韦弗联系了杰克的指挥官，并分享了他所知道的情况。

89
00:48:06.000 --> 00:49:08.000
This got the ball rolling. A code of silence had prevented recruits from speaking up earlier, but after Troy Weaver reached out, the Marines opened an investigation into the allegations on November 5, 2015. Jake Weaver provided a statement, as did Amir Bormash. Two months later, the findings were submitted. The training regiments' executive officer found the evidence compelling enough for the drill instructors involved to be stood down from their duties, including Joseph Felix. But no action followed. Four months later, Joseph Felix was given the role of senior drill instructor for Platoon 3042. Rahil Siddiqui, a Pakistani-American Muslim, was assigned to this platoon, despite Felix's history of abusing Islamic recruits.
这推动了事情的发展。沉默准则曾阻止新兵早些时候发声，但在特洛伊·韦弗联系后，海军陆战队于2015年11月5日对这些指控展开了调查。杰克·韦弗提供了陈述，阿米尔·博马什也提供了陈述。两个月后，调查结果被提交。训练团的执行官认为证据足以让相关教官停职，包括约瑟夫·菲利克斯。但随后没有采取任何行动。四个月后，约瑟夫·菲利克斯被任命为3042排的高级教官。拉希尔·西迪基，一名巴基斯坦裔美国穆斯林，被分配到这个排，尽管菲利克斯有虐待伊斯兰新兵的历史。

90
00:49:08.000 --> 00:50:11.000
On Thursday, March 17, 2016, an individual involved in the 2015 hazing investigation contacted the investigating officer to suggest more witnesses be interviewed. An email had just arrived from someone corroborating some of the most serious allegations. The following day was the day that Rahil died. Many of the recruits from Rahil's platoon noticed how Gunnery Sergeant Joseph Felix seemed to single Rahil out. Some heard him call Rahil a terrorist again and again in a completely serious tone. One recruit estimated that in just a few days of training, Felix addressed Rahil as a terrorist more than 10 times. In one meeting, he told Rahil that he smelled like a terrorist. At another, Felix asked the recruits if any of them knew what a bazaar was.
2016年3月17日星期四，一名参与2015年欺凌调查的人员联系了调查官，建议采访更多证人。一封来自某人的电子邮件刚刚送达，证实了一些最严重的指控。第二天就是拉希尔去世的日子。拉希尔排里的许多新兵注意到炮兵中士约瑟夫·菲利克斯似乎专门针对拉希尔。有些人听到他以完全严肃的语气一遍又一遍地称拉希尔为恐怖分子。一名新兵估计，在短短几天的训练中，菲利克斯称呼拉希尔为恐怖分子的次数超过10次。在一次会议上，他告诉拉希尔他闻起来像个恐怖分子。在另一次会议上，菲利克斯问新兵们是否有人知道什么是集市。

91
00:50:11.000 --> 00:51:09.000
Rahil said that he did. Of course you do, you goddamn terrorist, Felix replied. He also asked him if he needed his turban. At least one of the other recruits noticed that Rahil seemed reluctant to obey Felix's commands after being spoken to this way. Just the day after joining Felix's platoon, Rahil mentioned wanting to kill himself. Felix attended a meeting where Rahil discussed what he'd said, even though it was usual protocol for drill instructors to wait outside such meetings. Reports as to what exactly occurred in the immediate lead-up to Rahil's death were mixed. Some of his platoon mates who'd witnessed Felix reprimanding him said Felix had ordered Rahil to run while choking his own throat.
拉希尔说他知道。菲利克斯回答说，你当然知道，你这个该死的恐怖分子。他还问他是否需要他的头巾。至少有一名其他新兵注意到，在被这样对待后，拉希尔似乎不愿服从菲利克斯的命令。就在加入菲利克斯排的第二天，拉希尔提到了想自杀。菲利克斯参加了一次会议，会上拉希尔讨论了他所说的话，尽管教官在这些会议外等待是通常的规程。关于拉希尔死亡前夕究竟发生了什么，报道不一。一些目睹菲利克斯训斥他的排友说，菲利克斯命令拉希尔在掐住自己喉咙的同时奔跑。

92
00:51:09.000 --> 00:52:09.000
Others thought Rahil was holding his throat because it was sore. One witness said he'd seen Felix throw Rahil to the floor. The others all believed Rahil had collapsed on his own. Everyone agreed that Felix had slapped Rahil, but some thought he did so only once to revive him. Others said Felix slapped him hard two or three times. After that, Rahil had leapt up and sprinted out of the squad bay and over a stairwell. He died just five days after being assigned to Felix's platoon. On Thursday, September 8, 2016, six months after Rahil's death, the Marines released a 133-page report about the matter and other allegations of abuse.
其他人认为拉希尔捂着喉咙是因为喉咙痛。一名目击者说他看到菲利克斯把拉希尔扔到地板上。其他人则认为拉希尔是自己倒下的。每个人都同意菲利克斯扇了拉希尔耳光，但有些人认为他只是扇了一次以唤醒他。其他人则说菲利克斯用力扇了他两三次。在那之后，拉希尔跳起来冲出了宿舍区，越过了楼梯间。他在被分配到菲利克斯排仅五天后就去世了。2016年9月8日星期四，在拉希尔去世六个月后，海军陆战队发布了一份关于此事及其他虐待指控的133页报告。

93
00:52:09.000 --> 00:53:18.000
Much of it was redacted, with 40 pages completely blacked out. Nevertheless, it was clear the Marines had concluded that the actions of Joseph Felix directly led to Rahil jumping from the building. They also stated that Felix should never have been assigned to Rahil's platoon, given he was already under investigation for harassing another Muslim recruit. It was recommended that Felix be charged with assault for slapping Rahil. The report also focused on incidents involving other recruits being choked and forced to engage in unauthorized incentive training. It found Marines working as drill instructors had been operating with impunity without the proper supervision or leadership. 20 Marines were relieved of duty in the wake of the investigation, including three teams of drill instructors and the depot's regimental commander. Four were charged for incidents of abuse unrelated to Rahil Siddiqui.
其中大部分内容被删减，有40页完全涂黑。尽管如此，很明显海军陆战队得出的结论是，约瑟夫·菲利克斯的行为直接导致了拉希尔从楼上跳下。他们还指出，鉴于菲利克斯已经在接受骚扰另一名穆斯林新兵的调查，他不应该被分配到拉希尔的排。建议以扇拉希尔耳光为由对菲利克斯提出袭击指控。报告还重点关注了涉及其他新兵被掐脖子和被迫进行未经授权的惩罚性训练的事件。报告发现，担任教官的海军陆战队员在没有适当监督或领导的情况下肆无忌惮地行事。调查后，20名海军陆战队员被免职，包括三组教官和基地的团长。四人因与拉希尔·西迪基无关的虐待事件受到指控。

94
00:53:18.000 --> 00:54:40.000
Joseph Felix was charged with failure to obey a general order, cruelty and maltreatment, making a false statement, and drunk and disorderly conduct. Rahil's family were disappointed with the charges. They didn't understand why Felix wasn't charged with assault, as the report had recommended. Joseph Felix was ordered to face a military trial, which began in November 2017. The trial would not center on the death of Rahil Siddiqui, but focus on numerous allegations regarding Felix's treatment of recruits. The prosecution called almost 70 witnesses to the stand. Other drill instructors testified about behavior they'd witnessed from Felix. Various recruits spoke of him choking them, hitting them against walls and forcing them to hurt one another. The prosecution also detailed how Felix had seemingly targeted Muslim recruits, describing his actions as hate crimes. Amir Bormesh and Rakan Haverz spoke of how Felix had abused them for being Muslim, with both of them being forced into industrial dryers.
约瑟夫·菲利克斯被控不服从一般命令、残忍和虐待、作虚假陈述以及醉酒和扰乱治安。拉希尔的家人对这些指控感到失望。他们不明白为什么菲利克斯没有像报告建议的那样被控袭击罪。约瑟夫·菲利克斯被命令接受军事审判，审判于2017年11月开始。审判的重点不是拉希尔·西迪基的死亡，而是关于菲利克斯对待新兵的众多指控。检方传唤了近70名证人出庭。其他教官作证说他们目睹了菲利克斯的行为。多名新兵讲述了他掐他们、把他们撞向墙壁并强迫他们互相伤害。检方还详细描述了菲利克斯似乎如何针对穆斯林新兵，将其行为描述为仇恨犯罪。阿米尔·博马什和拉坎·哈维兹讲述了菲利克斯如何因为他们是穆斯林而虐待他们，两人都被强迫进入工业烘干机。

95
00:54:40.000 --> 00:55:53.000
Amir said Felix had tumbled him in the dryer for up to 30 seconds at a time. An expert on industrial dryers confirmed that a model such as the one in the 3rd Battalion's laundry was large enough to hold and tumble a recruit weighing up to 168 pounds. The defence only called one expert witness a burns expert. She said that in 30 seconds the dryer would have reached temperatures over 300 degrees Fahrenheit or 149 degrees Celsius. This would have caused third or fourth degree burns within one second, yet Amir had no physical evidence of burns. However, the expert did acknowledge that shorter durations could still cause pain without leaving visible injuries, adding, If I were in a dryer, 3 seconds would seem like an eternity. Although some said Felix spoke openly about his dislike of Muslims, Felix's lawyer insisted that his client hadn't specifically targeted Muslim recruits.
阿米尔说菲利克斯曾让他一次在烘干机里翻滚长达30秒。一位工业烘干机专家证实，像第三营洗衣房里的那种型号，大到足以容纳并翻滚一名重达168磅的新兵。辩方只传唤了一名专家证人，即烧伤专家。她说，在30秒内，烘干机的温度将达到华氏300度（149摄氏度）以上。这会在一秒钟内导致三度或四度烧伤，但阿米尔身上没有烧伤的物理证据。然而，专家确实承认，较短的时间仍然可能在不留下可见伤害的情况下造成疼痛，并补充说，如果我在烘干机里，3秒钟似乎就像永恒。虽然有人说菲利克斯公开谈论他对穆斯林的厌恶，但菲利克斯的律师坚称他的客户并没有专门针对穆斯林新兵。

96
00:55:53.000 --> 00:57:05.000
He had only discussed the Islamic faith with Amir out of curiosity, and he had chosen Rakan Haverz to be squad leader after discovering he was Muslim. Some witnesses suggested that Felix had only called Muslim recruits terrorists as a joke and hadn't meant anything by it at all. The eight-person jury made up of male Marines spent a day deliberating before reaching a verdict. They found Felix guilty of eight counts of violating training orders regarding multiple recruits, including slapping Raheel and forcing him to sprint laps while sick. But he was found not guilty of referring to Raheel as a terrorist. Felix was also convicted for being drunk and disorderly and making false official statements. But he was cleared of obstructing justice for supposedly telling recruits to conceal information about what happened to Raheel. During his sentencing, Joseph Felix addressed the court.
他只是出于好奇与阿米尔讨论了伊斯兰信仰，并且在发现拉坎·哈维兹是穆斯林后选择他担任班长。一些证人暗示，菲利克斯称穆斯林新兵为恐怖分子只是开玩笑，根本没有恶意。由八名男性海军陆战队员组成的陪审团在达成裁决前审议了一天。他们认定菲利克斯犯有八项违反训练命令的罪名，涉及多名新兵，包括扇拉希尔耳光和强迫他在生病时进行冲刺跑。但他被判无罪，罪名是称拉希尔为恐怖分子。菲利克斯还因醉酒和扰乱治安以及作虚假官方陈述而被定罪。但他被免除了妨碍司法的指控，因为他被指控告诉新兵隐瞒关于拉希尔身上发生的事情的信息。在量刑期间，约瑟夫·菲利克斯向法庭发表了讲话。

97
00:57:05.000 --> 00:57:54.000
He apologized to his wife, stating, Thank you for standing by me and being as wonderful as you are. I can never repay the disappointment I feel you have in me. He did not apologize to the Siddiqui family or the other recruits he had abused, nor did he acknowledge any of the charges he'd been convicted of. Felix's attorney asked that his client only serve 30 days in prison while the prosecution asked for seven years. He was sentenced to 10 years. His rank would also be reduced. He would have to forfeit all pay and allowances and would subsequently be given a dishonorable discharge.
他向妻子道歉，说，谢谢你支持我，你真是太棒了。我永远无法偿还你对我感到的失望。他没有向西迪基一家或其他被他虐待的新兵道歉，也没有承认他被定罪的任何指控。菲利克斯的律师要求他的客户只在监狱服刑30天，而检方要求判处七年。他被判处10年监禁。他的军衔也将被降低。他将不得不没收所有工资和津贴，并随后被非荣誉退伍。

98
00:57:54.000 --> 00:58:50.000
A total of five Marines ended up being convicted or pleading guilty to charges relating to hazing of recruits of Parris Island. Raheel Siddiqui's death wasn't the first time a recruit died at the depot. In 1956, a drill instructor ordered his platoon to march across a swamp. Six recruits drowned. Two decades later, another recruit was beaten with training sticks and subsequently died. Raheel's death had a ripple effect throughout the United States. Then President Barack Obama had his attention drawn to the case. A Democratic Congresswoman from Detroit reached out to the Siddiquis and petitioned the Marines on their behalf for an unbiased inquiry into hazing.
总共有五名海军陆战队员最终因与帕里斯岛新兵欺凌相关的指控被定罪或认罪。拉希尔·西迪基的死亡并不是该基地第一次有新兵死亡。1956年，一名教官命令他的排穿过一片沼泽。六名新兵溺水身亡。二十年后，另一名新兵被训练棍殴打后死亡。拉希尔的死在美国引起了连锁反应。时任总统巴拉克·奥巴马关注了此案。底特律的一位民主党女国会议员联系了西迪基一家，并代表他们向海军陆战队请愿，要求对欺凌行为进行公正的调查。

99
00:58:50.000 --> 01:00:02.000
In the wake of Raheel's death, Marine Corps Commandant General Robert Kneller, the highest-ranking official in the Marines, stated, We mourn the loss of recruits, Siddiqui, and we will take every step necessary to prevent tragic events like this from happening again. One of Raheel's platoon mates told The New York Times that despite some changes to training, he and the other recruits were still treated badly even after Raheel's death. Let's say you did report something, he said. They changed the DI, and what happens after that? Another DI, who presumably was friends with the prior DI, is going to make your life hell. Several months after Raheel died, a new commanding general was appointed to the Paris Island depot. Austin Renforth said about making changes, including having officers supervise drill instructors more actively and updating a policy letter to emphasize the Marines' zero-tolerance approach to hazing.
在拉希尔去世后，海军陆战队司令罗伯特·内勒将军，即海军陆战队最高级别的官员，表示，我们哀悼新兵西迪基的离世，我们将采取一切必要措施防止此类悲剧再次发生。拉希尔的一名排友告诉《纽约时报》，尽管训练有所改变，但即使在拉希尔死后，他和新兵们仍然受到恶劣对待。他说，假设你确实举报了什么，他们换了教官，那之后会发生什么？另一位大概是前教官朋友的教官会让你的生活变成地狱。拉希尔去世几个月后，一位新的指挥官被任命为帕里斯岛基地。奥斯汀·伦福斯谈到做出改变，包括让军官更积极地监督教官，并更新政策信以强调海军陆战队对欺凌行为的零容忍态度。

100
01:00:02.000 --> 01:01:11.000
In an interview with The New York Times, he admitted that he'd thought about contacting Raheel's parents but decided, quote, I just didn't feel it was my place. The Siddiqui struggled with the silence they received from the Marines after Raheel died. His sister, Sidra, told the Detroit Free Press newspaper that she now had difficulty saying the Pledge of Allegiance, a patriotic verse that students at most American public schools have to recite. Her faith in the country her parents had immigrated to for a better life had been broken. The Siddiquis chose not to speak to most reporters as they were disappointed with the way their son had been portrayed in the media, as though he were weak or unprepared for boot camp. In order to be accepted as a recruit, he'd had to pass a psychological exam. None of them had ever witnessed any signs pointing to Raheel having a mental illness or suicidal thoughts.
在接受《纽约时报》采访时，他承认他曾想过联系拉希尔的父母，但决定，引用他的话，我只是觉得那不是我的位置。西迪基一家在拉希尔死后从海军陆战队那里感受到的沉默中挣扎。他的妹妹西德拉告诉《底特律自由报》，她现在很难说出效忠誓词，这是大多数美国公立学校学生必须背诵的爱国诗句。她对父母为了更好的生活而移民的国家所持有的信念已经破灭。西迪基一家选择不与大多数记者交谈，因为他们对儿子在媒体上的形象感到失望，仿佛他很软弱或没有为新兵训练营做好准备。为了被接受为新兵，他必须通过心理测试。他们中没有人见过任何迹象表明拉希尔有精神疾病或自杀念头。

101
01:01:11.000 --> 01:02:26.000
They remain convinced that Raheel would never take his own life and believe there are unanswered questions relating to his death. The family lodged a civil suit suing the federal government for $100 million for their son's death. Their lawyer was arguing that the Marines had been negligent when recruiting Raheel in failing to tell him there had been allegations of abuse against Muslim recruits at Paris Island. At a time when the Marine Corps was eager to attract recruits from more diverse backgrounds, it seemed they had a duty of care to ensure those recruits would be safe from possible hate crimes. The Siddiquis also wanted Raheel's death certificate amended. A coroner had marked his cause of death as suicide, but his family thought it should be listed as undetermined. Because of the way Raheel's fate tripped over the stairwell causing him to fall awkwardly, it wasn't clear whether he had truly intended to take his own life. Perhaps he'd just been trying to escape Joseph Felix.
他们仍然坚信拉希尔永远不会自杀，并认为关于他的死亡还有未解之谜。家人提起民事诉讼，就儿子的死亡向联邦政府索赔1亿美元。他们的律师辩称，海军陆战队在招募拉希尔时存在疏忽，没有告诉他帕里斯岛曾有针对穆斯林新兵的虐待指控。在海军陆战队渴望吸引更多不同背景的新兵时，他们似乎有责任确保这些新兵免受可能的仇恨犯罪伤害。西迪基一家还希望修改拉希尔的死亡证明。验尸官将他的死因标记为自杀，但他的家人认为应该列为未定。由于拉希尔在楼梯间绊倒导致他笨拙地坠落，不清楚他是否真的打算自杀。也许他只是想逃离约瑟夫·菲利克斯。

